WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.496 --> 00:00:02.065
(crowd cheering)

00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:03.666
NARRATOR:
It's 1992,

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:07.003
President George H.W. Bush
is up for re-election.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.538
With a squeaky clean image,

00:00:08.605 --> 00:00:10.506
he's had some of the highest
approval ratings

00:00:10.573 --> 00:00:11.975
of any president.

00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:15.244
Then, a political bad boy
joins the race.

00:00:15.311 --> 00:00:17.714
(jazzy saxophone music)

00:00:19.983 --> 00:00:21.517
AJ BENZA:
Bill Clinton came on the scene.

00:00:21.584 --> 00:00:23.753
A young guy,
the next Kennedy,

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.421
handsome, charismatic.

00:00:28.658 --> 00:00:30.760
ICE-T: Clinton's over here
playing the saxophone.

00:00:30.827 --> 00:00:32.829
I'm like, oh,
this dude is smooth.

00:00:32.895 --> 00:00:34.297
This dude is a real player.

00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:36.265
NARRATOR:
He may be smooth,

00:00:36.332 --> 00:00:38.034
but Clinton will need
some serious help

00:00:38.101 --> 00:00:39.769
in a presidential race
that promises

00:00:39.836 --> 00:00:41.871
to be anything but boring.

00:00:41.938 --> 00:00:44.374
CONNIE CHUNG: Scandal wasn't
a new thing in politics,

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.177
but nothing was like Clinton
when he was first running

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:49.579
for president
of the United States.

00:00:50.279 --> 00:00:51.280
BILL CLINTON:
Come on.

00:00:51.414 --> 00:00:52.882
JOE KLEIN:
In the old days,

00:00:52.949 --> 00:00:55.518
there was one news cycle
a day. (laughs)

00:00:55.585 --> 00:00:57.954
There was the evening news
on television.

00:00:58.755 --> 00:01:00.657
KURT ANDERSEN:
Only during Clinton's campaign

00:01:00.723 --> 00:01:04.494
did we start getting
the 24/7 news cycle

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.464
that previous candidates
didn't have to deal with.

00:01:11.668 --> 00:01:13.169
NARRATOR: Clinton needs
a team to stay on top

00:01:13.236 --> 00:01:15.705
of the news coverage,
ready to spin the story.

00:01:15.772 --> 00:01:18.141
The leaders are
young communications director

00:01:18.207 --> 00:01:19.509
George Stephanopoulos...

00:01:19.876 --> 00:01:21.477
GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS:
That's what the American
people care about.

00:01:21.544 --> 00:01:23.012
They wanna move
into the future.

00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:24.781
NARRATOR:
...and their greatest weapon,

00:01:24.847 --> 00:01:26.949
political consultant
James Carville,

00:01:27.016 --> 00:01:29.919
known throughout Washington
as the Ragin' Cajun.

00:01:30.653 --> 00:01:32.188
CARVILLE: I've always said
a political campaign

00:01:32.255 --> 00:01:33.756
is like you've
kicked down a door,

00:01:33.823 --> 00:01:34.957
you don't know
what's behind it.

00:01:35.024 --> 00:01:37.293
NARRATOR: Carville's a genius
at political strategy

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.229
and keeping the campaign
on message.

00:01:40.296 --> 00:01:41.831
CARVILLE: Stay focused,
talk about things

00:01:41.898 --> 00:01:43.066
that matter to people,

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:44.801
you know.

00:01:45.268 --> 00:01:46.636
It's the economy, stupid.

00:01:48.571 --> 00:01:50.139
NARRATOR:
Combative and loud,

00:01:50.206 --> 00:01:51.507
he ushers in a new era

00:01:51.574 --> 00:01:53.843
of political
hand-to-hand combat,

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.511
organized from his war room.

00:01:55.845 --> 00:01:58.514
CARVILLE:
The war room was conceived

00:01:58.581 --> 00:02:01.651
to deal with...
to compress news cycles

00:02:02.151 --> 00:02:04.654
in a coherent
and coordinated way.

00:02:05.121 --> 00:02:06.489
GEORGE BUSH SR.:
And I will stand on my record,

00:02:06.556 --> 00:02:08.991
and I won't let
that Arkansas governor

00:02:09.058 --> 00:02:10.693
run away
from his record either.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:12.328
(crowd cheering)

00:02:12.395 --> 00:02:13.763
NARRATOR:
When Bush attacks,

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.265
Clinton's war room ignores
the old tactic

00:02:16.332 --> 00:02:18.501
of letting bad stories
blow over

00:02:18.568 --> 00:02:20.403
and goes on the offensive.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:23.206
CARVILLE: What are we gonna do
when George Bush attacks us?

00:02:23.272 --> 00:02:25.408
Why can't we attack
George Bush?

00:02:25.475 --> 00:02:26.943
NEWS ANCHOR:
Today, Governor Clinton accused

00:02:27.009 --> 00:02:30.213
the president's party
of misrepresenting his past.

00:02:30.279 --> 00:02:31.481
Here's ABC's Jim Wooten.

00:02:31.948 --> 00:02:33.516
CARVILLE:
The idea was to answer somethin'

00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:35.551
in a creative,
a provocative way,

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:40.790
that editors would see
and lead with that story.

